{
  "domain": "TRUEOPEN_TASK_BUILDER_RANK_V1",
  "notes": [
    "H_FIELDS_V1(\"TRUEOPEN_TASK_BUILDER_RANK_V1\", task_builder_seed, builder_operator_address). Two fields, in that order; the registry row names both.",
    "builder_operator_address frames the address codec bytes, never the Bech32 text (Decision 24). The bech32 column is a self-check so a non-Go implementation can validate its own decoder here instead of discovering a broken one as a digest mismatch.",
    "The vectors share one seed and differ only in the Builder, which is what the rank is for: one task_builder_seed maps every candidate Builder onto its own rank, and selection is the ascending order of those ranks.",
    "This file used to publish (seed, address) -\u003e rank pairs with no per-vector preimage, so the rank VALUES were pinned but the field ORDER was not: swapping the two fields inside the producer would have moved every rank and agreed with a regenerated file. The preimage below is what the root differential compares against the registry row."
  ],
